 "max_plain_reason": "A plain word fits two short lines in a launcher tile in every language; the fit guard checks the layout itself.",
 "retired_note": "Names banned outright (core/naming.py BANNED) are never written anywhere, not even here; a screen that showed one would fail as an unknown name.",
 "icons_rule": "Each name shows its own product mark from the brand module (brand.icon), a service, feature or card group without one its product's mark, and a device none. A new name's mark is released in lynkomni-icons in the same build section that adds the name.",
 "spoken_rule": "How to say each name, for voice menus on basic phones, LynkAssist's voice and the note screen readers read. Lynk is said as the English word link; the letters of a short capital part are said one by one in the listener's language.",
 "now_called": [
  {
   "old": "LynkDash",
   "id": "stat",
   "since": "2026-11-08"
  },
  {
   "old": "LynkLedger",
   "id": "acc",
   "since": "2026-11-07"
  }
 ],
 "now_called_rule": "A retired name with a successor still finds the new name in search with a short \"now called\" note, and a person whose account is older than the change sees a one-time notice. A retired name appears only there; retired names without a successor are never shown. A renamed product adds its line here in the same change.",
